ng Akhshunwar helps <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> gain the Sasanian throne from his brother.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">474</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> begins three wars against his former allies; captured in the first two, he pays thirty mules loaded with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> drachms and leaves his son Kavad as a hostage.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">484</span><span class="rf-text">At the Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herat">Herat</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> is defeated and killed by the Hephthalite king Kun-khi; for two years the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> plunder and control the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">488</span><span class="rf-text">A Hephthalite army defeats the Sasanian army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balash">Balash</a> and places <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I</a>, who had lived four years among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a>, on the throne.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">509</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> capture Sughd, the capital of Sogdiana, and push north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turfan">Turfan</a> to the Urumchi region in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">516</span><span class="rf-text">King Yilituo Yandai sends the first Hephthalite ambassador to the Southern Liang court, recorded in the Portraits of Periodical Offering of Liang.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">557</span><span class="rf-text">The Turks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fir